lly improved through the\nquarter (92.1% in May to 97.7% in July), so service quality isn't a concern.\nCosts were essentially flat all quarter, which is good discipline, but it\nalso means margin is now fully exposed to top-line swings — there's no cost\nbuffer absorbing the July revenue miss.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false}}
